PATCH 361: editor .FSG load->save ROUND-TRIP harness (env-gated FIST_FSG_ROUNDTRIP, DEFAULT OFF).

A DIAGNOSTIC/harness hook (like patch 172), NOT a covered flow-change: with FIST_FSG_ROUNDTRIP set,
the BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT cascade -- after FUN_0000_4754 has run FUN_0000_d501 to LOAD the selected
.FSG into the battle-state DGROUP + live unit list, and BEFORE FUN_1000_6015 and the e4bb game loop
-- drives the engine's OWN serializer FUN_0000_d5f9 (patch 360) to re-save the battle to the loaded
filename (DGROUP:0x79a9), then exit(0).  Firing at this point (0 sim ticks elapsed) makes the re-save
the DETERMINISTIC pristine post-load state: reproducible, byte-stable, and identical native<->wasm.

WHY A FIXED-POINT AND NOT AN ORIGINAL-FILE COMPARE: the LOAD handler d81e (asm 0xd847 `pop 0x2(%di)`)
deliberately restores each unit's data+2 field to the value FUN_1000_bb12 recomputes from the record
(idx/val), DISCARDING the file's stored data+2.  This is faithful engine behaviour, so an editor-
authored .FSG is NOT itself a fixed point of load->save (its data+2 differs).  But load->save is
IDEMPOTENT: a re-saved file reloads + re-saves byte-identically.  The editor-fsg-roundtrip verify
flow proves it: (A) load(orig AZER1.FSG)->save = file1; (B) load(file1)->save = file2; file1==file2,
native AND wasm, native file1==wasm file1.

Gated behind getenv (NULL by default; getenv/exit via ghidra_compat.h <stdlib.h>, ENV mirrored to
wasm by tools/wasm_pre.js) -> the 26 verify flows never set it -> BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL, verify.sh
unchanged.  4754 is only reached on the ACCEPT cascade; the hook precedes the sim so no gameplay
state is perturbed.  asm-verified callee (d5f9, patch 360) vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.

